{%- comment -%}
  Customer reviews — Judge.me (owner's choice, Sep 2026; free plan).

  Judge.me owns everything here: collecting reviews (its emails ask
  buyers after delivery, and its widget has a "Write a review" form with
  photo and video upload), moderation, and display. The theme only gives
  the widget its place on the page — after "You may also like" and
  "Recently viewed" — and a heading in the site's own type.

  Two ways the widget can arrive, either is fine:
  · Judge.me's app block, added to this section in the theme editor
    (Customize → Product page → SV Reviews → Add block → Judge.me). When
    one is present it is used and nothing else renders.
  · Otherwise the classic Judge.me widget element below, which Judge.me
    fills in on every product page once the app is installed and its
    "Judge.me Core" app embed is on (Customize → App embeds).

  With Judge.me not installed, the section renders nothing on the live
  site — no placeholder stars, no sample reviews (ARCHITECTURE §27.2);
  the theme editor shows a one-line hint instead.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign app_block = false
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == '@app'
      assign app_block = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
  assign jm_installed = false
  if product.metafields.judgeme != blank or shop.metafields.judgeme != blank
    assign jm_installed = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if app_block or jm_installed or request.design_mode -%}
  <section class="sv-reviews" id="reviews" data-sv>
    <div class="w">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="sv-reviews__h">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if app_block -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {% render block %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <div id="judgeme_product_reviews" class="jdgm-widget jdgm-review-widget jdgm-outside-widget" data-id="{{ product.id }}">
          {{- product.metafields.judgeme.widget -}}
        </div>
        {%- if request.design_mode and jm_installed == false -%}
          <p class="sv-reviews__hint">Install Judge.me Product Reviews (free plan) and turn on its app embed — the reviews widget appears here.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  section[data-sv].sv-reviews {
    padding: var(--d) 0 0;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-reviews__h {
    margin: 0 0 var(--c);
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-reviews__hint {
    padding: var(--b);
    border: 1px dashed var(--tan);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* Judge.me in the site's palette: gold stars, emerald actions. Only
     colour — its layout is left alone. */
  .sv-reviews .jdgm-star,
  .sv-pdp__rating .jdgm-star {
    color: var(--tan) !important;
  }

  .sv-reviews .jdgm-write-rev-link,
  .sv-reviews .jdgm-submit-rev,
  .sv-reviews .jdgm-ask-question-btn {
    border-color: var(--emerald) !important;
    background: var(--emerald) !important;
    color: var(--cream) !important;
  }

  /* The section already has its heading. */
  .sv-reviews .jdgm-rev-widg__title {
    display: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Reviews",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Customer reviews" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Reviews come from Judge.me. Install 'Judge.me Product Reviews' (free plan) and switch on its 'Judge.me Core' app embed; the widget then shows here automatically. You can also add Judge.me's review widget block to this section instead." }
  ],
  "blocks": [{ "type": "@app" }],
  "presets": [{ "name": "SV Reviews" }]
}
{% endschema %}
